   "text": "The stop fired correctly. The search has concluded. The best support reached was [9-, 7-] with in-sample Sharpe 1.1986 (the 3-feature extension didn't help, confirming the 2-feature spec is the local optimum reached via a legitimate, pre-declared stopping rule).\n\nNow let me submit this specification. I need to think carefully about the out-of-sample Sharpe prediction:\n\n- In-sample Sharpe of 1.1986 was achieved via greedy search (init + 1 extend) over 80 candidate features, with costs already netted out (5bps turnover, 50bps borrow, 1-day lag).\n- This is a very short search (only 2 content moves kept), which limits overfitting compared to exhaustive search, but there's still selection bias from `init` scanning all 80 single-feature/sign candidates and `extend_best` scanning ~78 pairs.\n- Realistic expectation: out-of-sample Sharpe typically degrades substantially from in-sample due to selection bias, regime change, and the fact that this is a daily equity-like return panel with only 40 instruments/40 features \u2014 multiple testing haircut is significant even for a 2-feature spec.\n- I'll estimate the OOS Sharpe mean to be meaningfully lower than 1.20, perhaps around 0.5-0.6, with a wide standard deviation reflecting real uncertainty."
